WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.821 --> 00:00:17.868
The hoof beasts carried Zann and his friends away from the rocky gully into more sand dunes.

2
00:00:18.788 --> 00:00:20.969
Then they passed some scrubby trees.

3
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.492
After that they crossed the grassland Darb and Perda had mentioned.

4
00:00:26.332 --> 00:00:28.013
More hoof beasts were grazing there.

5
00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:32.316
"Let's look over there," Perda called, pointing to some hills.

6
00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:37.174
They rode to the hills, which at first were gently rolling and mostly sand.

7
00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:42.816
Then the slopes got steeper and rockier, with a few plants dotted here and there.

8
00:00:44.037 --> 00:00:45.477
Perda peered into a cave.

9
00:00:45.497 --> 00:00:49.359
"How are we supposed to find two people around here?"

10
00:00:49.659 --> 00:00:50.039
she said.

11
00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:52.240
"They could be anywhere.

12
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.821
Maybe we should try using magic."

13
00:00:54.841 --> 00:01:01.064
"Maybe," Zann said, remembering what had happened with the levitation spell and the airberry juice.

14
00:01:01.836 --> 00:01:07.678
"But we'll have to be careful because—" A Red Share hit Zann, almost knocking him off his hoof

15
00:01:07.698 --> 00:01:09.798
beast. It was from Gliss.

16
00:01:10.639 --> 00:01:11.619
She was terrified!

17
00:01:11.639 --> 00:01:14.940
"Zann!" Darb halted his hoof beast.

18
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.240
"Are you okay?"

19
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.621
Zann gulped for breath as the Red Share started to fade.

20
00:01:20.641 --> 00:01:23.542
"I'm fine," he said.

21
00:01:23.562 --> 00:01:25.203
"But I'm not sure about Gliss."

22
00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:27.263
He told them about the Share.

23
00:01:27.283 --> 00:01:29.024
"Oh, no!"

24
00:01:29.444 --> 00:01:30.024
Perda cried.

25
00:01:30.688 --> 00:01:32.189
"We have to find her!"

26
00:01:32.209 --> 00:01:34.490
"Could you tell where it was coming from?"

27
00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:35.291
Darb asked.

28
00:01:36.311 --> 00:01:37.472
Zann closed his eyes.

29
00:01:38.312 --> 00:01:41.254
He could still feel Gliss' terror in the back of his mind.

30
00:01:41.994 --> 00:01:43.815
He turned his head, and it faded.

31
00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:48.057
When he turned his head the other way, the Share got a little stronger.

32
00:01:48.878 --> 00:01:49.698
He opened his eyes.

33
00:01:49.718 --> 00:01:52.360
"That way, I think," he said, pointing.

34
00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.761
"I hope Gliss is all right."

35
00:01:55.321 --> 00:01:56.262
Darb sounded worried.

36
00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:59.944
"I wonder if Wyssa is with her," Perda said.

37
00:02:00.744 --> 00:02:03.606
"If not, then maybe that's why she's scared."

38
00:02:04.447 --> 00:02:05.187
Darb nodded.

39
00:02:05.207 --> 00:02:09.530
"I'd be scared too, if I were all alone in the Far Frontier."

40
00:02:10.491 --> 00:02:11.692
Zann didn't say anything.

41
00:02:12.552 --> 00:02:15.975
Gliss hadn't just felt scared—she'd felt terrified.

42
00:02:16.755 --> 00:02:19.077
Would she feel that way just from being alone?

43
00:02:19.877 --> 00:02:20.638
He wasn't sure.

44
00:02:21.518 --> 00:02:22.639
They emerged from the hills.

45
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.901
Ahead of them the desert stretched into the distance.

46
00:02:26.642 --> 00:02:29.304
Perda shaded her eyes against the blinding sunlight.

47
00:02:30.056 --> 00:02:32.597
"I don't see anything," she said.

48
00:02:33.477 --> 00:02:34.318
She looked anxious.

49
00:02:34.338 --> 00:02:35.958
"Or anyone.

50
00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:39.700
Do you really think Gliss could be anywhere out there?"

51
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.221
"Look." Darb pointed.

52
00:02:42.241 --> 00:02:44.402
"There are more hills over there."

53
00:02:45.302 --> 00:02:47.823
Zann squinted through the hot, hazy sunlight.

54
00:02:48.463 --> 00:02:51.445
"That's the direction the Share seems to be leading us," he said.

55
00:02:51.465 --> 00:02:52.925
"Come on, let's hurry."

56
00:02:53.946 --> 00:02:56.807
The hoof beasts seemed to sense the kids' urgency.

57
00:02:57.547 --> 00:02:59.328
The animals broke into a faster gait.

58
00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.562
Their hooves pounded the sand, kicking up clouds of dust.

59
00:03:04.442 --> 00:03:09.084
Zann held on to his beast's long, silky mane, hoping he wouldn’t bounce off.

60
00:03:09.104 --> 00:03:16.607
"At least Morb can't sneak up on us out here—there’s nowhere for him to hide," Perda joked weakly.

61
00:03:16.627 --> 00:03:19.108
"Why do you think he came here?"

62
00:03:19.768 --> 00:03:22.389
Zann glanced around at the sun-bleached sand.

63
00:03:22.409 --> 00:03:25.371
"Could he really be searching for the Source?"

64
00:03:25.391 --> 00:03:27.832
"Maybe." Darb shrugged.

65
00:03:28.556 --> 00:03:30.237
"That sounds like something he'd do."

66
00:03:30.257 --> 00:03:33.800
"Laddno will be mad if someone else finds it first."

67
00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.622
Zann tried to laugh at his own remark.

68
00:03:37.302 --> 00:03:40.224
But he was too worried about Gliss to do more than cough.

69
00:03:41.325 --> 00:03:43.066
They were nearing the next set of hills.

70
00:03:43.887 --> 00:03:50.351
The hills were steep and rocky, with spiky plants clinging to them and a few scrawny trees growing

71
00:03:50.451 --> 00:03:52.192
sideways out of pockets of soil.

72
00:03:52.893 --> 00:03:53.533
Perda looked up.

73
00:03:54.194 --> 00:03:57.016
"I'm not sure these beasts can climb these hills."

74
00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.121
"They won't have to climb them."

75
00:03:59.561 --> 00:04:00.222
Darb pointed.

76
00:04:00.242 --> 00:04:02.824
"I see a trail that leads up to the top."

77
00:04:03.904 --> 00:04:09.588
Zann followed as Darb and his hoof beast led the way into a narrow opening between two hills.

78
00:04:10.369 --> 00:04:14.392
The shade of the trail felt good after the searing heat of the desert sun.

79
00:04:15.173 --> 00:04:16.794
But Zann felt a little nervous.

80
00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:20.136
It was hard to see more than a few strides ahead.

81
00:04:20.897 --> 00:04:23.398
What if they ran into another sand beast in here?

82
00:04:24.079 --> 00:04:25.360
What if they ran into Morb?

83
00:04:26.076 --> 00:04:28.058
The hoof beasts seemed nervous too.

84
00:04:28.859 --> 00:04:32.502
Zann's beast, looking alert, had its head way up in the air.

85
00:04:33.323 --> 00:04:36.986
Its ears swiveled, and it let out a loud snort.

86
00:04:37.847 --> 00:04:42.191
Perda cried out as her beast suddenly jumped forward with its ears pricked.

87
00:04:43.252 --> 00:04:45.514
"Why are they acting like this?"

88
00:04:46.035 --> 00:04:46.735
she exclaimed.

89
00:04:47.716 --> 00:04:48.957
Darb patted his beast.

90
00:04:49.778 --> 00:04:51.660
Then he glanced back at the others.

91
00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.523
"Maybe the hoof beasts don't like being in such an enclosed space," he said.

92
00:04:56.543 --> 00:05:00.646
"They're used to being out in the open desert or grasslands.

93
00:05:01.446 --> 00:05:05.509
They're probably worried that—" He broke off with a strangled cry.

94
00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.031
Zann started to call to him.

95
00:05:08.772 --> 00:05:12.054
But before he could, he felt something tighten around his chest.

96
00:05:12.854 --> 00:05:13.535
It was a rope!

97
00:05:13.555 --> 00:05:15.977
"Hey!" Zann shouted.

98
00:05:16.577 --> 00:05:20.340
He tried to shake off the rope, but it was pinning his arms to his sides.

99
00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.524
A second later he felt the rope jerk him right off the hoof beast's back.

100
00:05:26.305 --> 00:05:28.306
He slammed into the rocky ground with a grunt.

101
00:05:29.227 --> 00:05:33.330
Out of the corner of his eye, Zann saw that both of his friends were in the same

102
00:05:33.391 --> 00:05:37.314
situation. He squirmed desperately, trying to free himself.

103
00:05:38.014 --> 00:05:41.637
But the rope was too tight—and it was thick and strong.

104
00:05:41.657 --> 00:05:44.240
"Someone lassoed us!"

105
00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:45.261
Perda cried.

106
00:05:45.281 --> 00:05:46.842
"Who was it?

107
00:05:47.522 --> 00:05:49.004
Hey, show yourselves!"

108
00:05:50.348 --> 00:05:53.749
Several people stepped out of the shadows of the rocky hills.

109
00:05:54.589 --> 00:05:56.310
The people were tall and lean.

110
00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:00.011
Their loose clothes were the same color as the sand.

111
00:06:00.851 --> 00:06:07.493
Wide-brimmed hats hid part of their faces, though Zann was pretty sure those faces were painted with clay

112
00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:08.134
or paint.

113
00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:11.655
He'd seen pictures of such tribes in his parents' book.

114
00:06:12.335 --> 00:06:15.776
They were nomads who were able to survive in this rough land.

115
00:06:16.604 --> 00:06:20.409
Zann watched nervously as one of the strangers stepped forward.

116
00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:24.875
"You should not have come here," the man said darkly.

117
00:06:24.895 --> 00:06:30.982
"Your friend has caused us great sorrow, and now you must die."
